=== parameters ===
panel 200 assets x 750 days; industries 10
DGP: r = beta_true*f_true + beta_mkt*f_mkt + beta_size*f_size + industry + noise
f_true has planted daily premium MU_TRUE=0.0025 (~63% ann per unit beta; exaggerated for teaching clarity)
raw_factor = beta_true + 0.4*industry + 0.25*size_loading + noise  (nuisance contamination)
look-ahead: factor[t] vs forward returns starting t+1; LS weights use shift(1); impact vol lagged
cite: Fama & MacBeth 1973 JPE 81(3) 607-636 — cross-section then time-series mean of slopes
cite: Fama & French 1993 JFE 33(1) 3-56 — Mkt-Rf, SMB, HML (FF3)
cite: Fama & French 2015 JFE 116(1) 1-22 — FF5 = FF3 + RMW + CMA
cite: Harvey, Liu & Zhu 2016 RFS 29(1) 5-68 — '...and the Cross-Section of Expected Returns'; t>3
cite: Alphalens Reloaded docs (alphalens.ml4trading.io) — get_clean_factor_and_forward_returns + tear sheets
cite: Qlib DataHandlerLP processors CSZScoreNorm / CSZFillna / Alpha158 (qlib.readthedocs.io)
niche: quant-wiki factor taxonomy as foil only; frontier LLM formulaic mining deferred to P8 (not re-run)

=== factor construction ===
mean_cs_corr(raw, beta_true)=0.7120
mean_cs_corr(z_only, beta_true)=0.7082
mean_cs_corr(neutralized, beta_true)=0.9194
teach: industry+mcap residualization lifts recovery of the planted loading

=== RankIC / ICIR / decay ===
RankIC h=1: mean=0.1105 std=0.3768 ICIR_ann≈4.654 n=749
RankIC h=5: mean=0.2268 std=0.3671 ICIR_ann≈4.386 n=745
RankIC h=10: mean=0.3055 std=0.3512 ICIR_ann≈4.367 n=740
RankIC h=20: mean=0.4109 std=0.2877 ICIR_ann≈5.069 n=730
ICIR_daily = mean/std * sqrt(252) = 4.654
decaying_alpha_foil RankIC h=1: mean=0.5995
decaying_alpha_foil RankIC h=5: mean=0.3449
decaying_alpha_foil RankIC h=10: mean=0.1813
decaying_alpha_foil RankIC h=20: mean=0.0440
teach: static risk loading → mean RankIC can RISE with cumulative horizon; decaying alpha FALLS — both are 'IC decay' lessons
