=== quintile portfolios (Alphalens-style long-short) ===
LS gross_SR=4.465 net_SR=3.734 mean_turn=0.9349 NAV_net=34.4183
cost model: P2 10 bps one-way + √impact with LAGGEDrolling σ (VOL_LB=20, shift(1), expanding warm-up)

=== Fama–MacBeth (single-factor CS slopes) ===
FM_daily mean_gamma=0.002119 t_iid=7.771 t_NeweyWest_L5=7.314 n=749
FM_monthly mean_gamma=0.043795 t_iid=7.893 t_NeweyWest_L3=10.984 n_months=34
FF3 (1993): Mkt-Rf, SMB, HML. FF5 (2015): + RMW, CMA. Lab FM uses the single planted factor.

=== factor zoo / Harvey–Liu–Zhu (2016) multiple testing ===
random_factors=200 frac_|t|>2=0.045 frac_|t|>3=0.000
true_factor_FM_daily_t=7.771 FM_monthly_t=7.893 (monthly should clear t>3 with planted premium)
Harvey et al. 2016: with a zoo of published factors, new claims should clear ~t>3, not t≈2

=== crowding / decay foil ===
factor_rank_autocorr_lag1_mean=0.8666
teach: high rank AC → lower theoretical turnover, but crowding if books converge; IC decay caps horizon

=== Alphalens/Qlib-style workflow (pandas) ===
steps: (1) clean factor + forward returns (2) RankIC series (3) quantile returns (4) turnover
optional API map: alphalens.utils.get_clean_factor_and_forward_returns → tears.create_information_tear_sheet / create_returns_tear_sheet
Qlib: DataHandlerLP + CSZScoreNorm / CSZFillna processors ≈ winsorize+z+neutralize here; Alpha158 is a feature set ref
